- Problem: Smart Complete V1/V2 still worked like a generic local fill and did not use NovaFlow split-layer context, so it could sample foreground occluders back into the current layer.
- Cause: executePenFillTool previously passed only the current layer crop and user mask into the fill algorithms. penSymmetryPatchCompleteFillCanvas / penSmartCompleteFillCanvas had no forbidden sampling mask, foreground alpha, layer-order context, same-group constraint, or single-side / dual-side reference state.
- Change: Only particle-editor/spine-split-runtime.js was modified. Added buildSplitCompleteContext, classifySplitCompleteStrategy, forbiddenMask / allowedSampleMask / occluderMask construction, and split-aware stats. The original sourceCanvas is context/reference only and is not used as a fill source. Patch candidates now come only from allowed current-layer sample pixels and exclude the user mask, foreground occluder alpha, transparent/low-alpha pixels, and non-same-group layer alpha.
- Strategy: small-hole uses patch-lite / edge fallback; single-side uses directional patch-lite / edge fallback; dual-side uses symmetry-patch / patch-lite / edge fallback; reference-insufficient does not write the layer and suggests AI inpaint. Existing mask-outside zero-change protection, layer undo/redo, AI inpaint, AI cutout, and PSD export paths were kept unchanged.
- Stats: mode=split-aware, strategy, algorithm, fallback, reason, maskPixels, forbiddenRatio, occluderPartIds, left/right/top/bottom source pixels, and allowedSamplePixels are exposed through splitRuntimeTrace and state.lastSmartCompleteStats.
- Validation: node --check particle-editor/spine-split-runtime.js PASS; npm run sync:runtime PASS, spine-split-runtime.js SHA256 ad523455226aa19473a63967b4a8f0920572e43fe1aa8cabf0c1da90da84587f; npm run check:runtime PASS; npm run check:entry PASS, locked 4783 Overall: GO.
- Risk: Occluder detection is inferred from layer order and alpha overlap, not semantic truth. Manual layer-order changes and custom naming can weaken same-group classification. Large reference-insufficient holes intentionally suggest AI inpaint instead of forcing a poor local fill.

[2026-06-08 16:18]

- Problem: Split-aware Smart Complete V3 could still produce mosaic/block artifacts on low-texture large-color regions such as skirts, capes, and sleeves because symmetry/patch-lite paths copy discrete blocks or source pixels.
- Cause: penSymmetryPatchCompleteFillCanvas writes 12/16/24px patch blocks and only blends repeated writes lightly; penSmartCompleteFillCanvas advances by copied source pixels. Neither path had a flat-region detector, four-side color interpolation, alpha continuation, or low-frequency smoothing for broad cloth shapes.
- Change: Only particle-editor/spine-split-runtime.js was manually modified. Added detectFlatShapeCompleteContext and penFlatShapeCompleteFillCanvas. classifySplitCompleteStrategy now detects strategy=flat-shape before small-hole / single-side / dual-side. executePenFillTool routes flat-shape to flat-shape-gradient completion.
- Flat-shape behavior: Uses current-layer allowedSampleMask only. The original sourceCanvas remains reference/context only and is not copied as fill source. The detector samples the mask ring, measures lumaVariance / rgbVariance / edgeDensity, prefers left/right or top/bottom side statistics for central cloth holes, then fills mask pixels with four-direction boundary color interpolation, alpha continuation, and 2-4 low-frequency smoothing passes. Patch is not used as the main fill source.
- Protection: Existing mergeHardMaskedCrop and mask-outside zero-change check remain unchanged. Existing layer undo/redo, AI inpaint, AI cutout, PSD export, layer selection, and mask drawing paths were not changed.
- Stats: Added strategy=flat-shape, algorithm=flat-shape-gradient, lumaVariance, edgeDensity, ringSampleCount, and smoothingPasses in __smartCompleteStats/state.lastSmartCompleteStats.
