- Problem: one-click SeeThrough split can spend a long time inside Runtime GPU stages, while the UI only shows a generic running timer and users can mistake it for a hang.
- Cause: runSeeThroughLayers only waited for the final history result, and the busy overlay had no prompt/queue state; SeeThrough v3 head/depth stages do not expose fine progress, so runtime can have non-linear long-tail latency.
- Fix: add SeeThrough prompt monitoring over /history/{promptId} and /queue, classify running/pending/missing/timeout states, and show mode, resolution, steps, Runtime state, long-running hints, and layer-read progress in the busy overlay.
- Scope: particle-editor/spine-split-runtime.js one-click SeeThrough split waiting and status UI only; no SeeThrough plugin, Runtime installer, model, workflow, or PSD postprocess changes.

